            <p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="2">The following policies apply to all &quot;.WS&quot; domain name registrations.&nbsp;</font>
            </p>
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">

<tr><td valign="top" width="100%">
<font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="#TRADEMARK">Trademark and Name Disputes</a></font></td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" width="100%">
<font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="#FEES">Registration, Renewal and Administrative Fees</a></font></td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" width="100%">
<font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="#AUP">Acceptable Use Policy</a></font></td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" width="100%">
<font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="#RESERVED">Reserved and Restricted Names</a></font></td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" width="100%"><p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/privacy.dhtml')">Privacy Policy</a></font></td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top" width="100%"><p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="#TERMSOFUSE">Terms of Use</a></font></td></tr>
</table>
<h3 align="left"><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><a name="TRADEMARK">Trademark and Name Disputes</a></font>
</h3>
            <ol>
              <li>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Registrant certifies that he or she has legal right to the name being registered, and that use of the domain name selected does not violate any copyrights, trademarks or service marks.</font>
              </li>
              <li>
                <font face="Arial" size="2">
                Registrant understands that WebSite.ws is not responsible for verifying ownership for any name registered, and
                that WebSite.ws will not become involved in any dispute over domain name registration rights.&nbsp;</font>
              </li>
              <li>
                <font face="Arial" size="2">In the event of a dispute over a domain name registration,  involvement will be limited to providing registrant contact information to the disputing
                party.&nbsp;</font>
</li>
</ol>
<p><font face="Arial" size="2">For full details, please view the full <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/dispute.html')"> Dispute Policy</a>.</font></p>
<h3><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><a name="FEES">Registration, Renewal and Administrative Fees</a></font></h3>
<ol>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">Domain name registration fees (based on the cost of the domain, see <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/costs.html')">rates</a>) must be paid in full for the entire initial registration period prior to domain activation.</font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">After the initial registration period, renewal fees (based on the cost of the domain, see <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/costs.html')">rates</a>) will be required. Failure to pay renewal fees by the expiration of the initial registration period or the prior renewal period will result in the domain being deactivated and made available for registration by others.</font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">When payment in full cannot be made online using a valid credit card, domains will be held in reserve to allow for payment to be mailed or faxed. Reserved domains will be held for 10 days if payment will be faxed or mailed. Domains in reserve will not be accessible to the Internet, but they will not be available for registration by others.</font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">Mailed payments may be in the form of a check written on a US bank in US dollars, or a money order for US dollars. Checks returned by the bank will be subject to a US$25 returned check fee.</font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2"><b>Domain registration fees are due immediately and are non-refundable.</b></font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">Registration periods purchased prior to an ownership transfer are automatically forfeited, and do not carry-over to the new owner. The new owner must complete payment for a new registration period within 10 days of the ownership transfer to retain ownership of the domain. Failure to complete this step will result in the release of the domain back into the general pool without compensation or refund.</font></li>
<li><font face="Arial" size="2">Domains that are transferred from one owner to another prior to the regular expiration of the initial registration period or a renewal period may be subject to an administrative transfer fee at the discretion of WebSite.ws.</font></li>
            </ol>
            <p><font face="Arial" size="2">For full details, please view the full <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/agreement.dhtml')">Domain Name Registration Agreement</a>.</font></p>
            <h3><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><a name="AUP">Acceptable Use Policy</a></font></h3>
            <ol>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">WebSite.ws is not responsible for the content or
                use of any .WS domain registered.</font></li>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">Under extreme circumstances, WebSite.ws reserves
                the right to suspend or permanently remove domains that are used
                for the purpose of sending Unsolicited Commercial Email (UCE)
                when such use may jeopardize the proper functioning of the .WS
                Top Level Domain.</font></li>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">WebSite.ws reserves the right to suspend or
                permanently disable domains that are used for illegal purposes
                or were obtained in a fraudulent manner.</font></li>
            </ol>
            <h3><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><a name="RESERVED">Reserved and Restricted Names</a></font></h3>
            <ol>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">WebSite.ws reserves the right to refuse to
                register any domain name that is, in  opinion,
                vulgar, obscene or generally offensive to most
                individuals.&nbsp;</font></li>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">Since the registration process is automated,
                WebSite.ws reserves the right to review domain names after they
                are registered. The owners of names found to be unsuitable after
                registration has been completed may register another name or
                request a refund of the registration fee.&nbsp;</font></li>
              <li><font face="Arial" size="2">Some domain names have
                been reserved by WebSite.ws and are not available for
		
                registration. Other domains may be similarly reserved for
                traditional and practical reasons.&nbsp;</font></li>
            </ol>
            <h3><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><b><a name="PRIVACY">Privacy Policy</a></b></font></h3>
            <p><font face="Arial" size="2"><b>WebSite.ws</b> believes that the privacy of
            both domain owners and visitors to its WebSite is of the utmost
            importance. For this reason we have established a comprehensive <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/privacy.dhtml')">Privacy
            Policy</a> to keep the public informed about what information is
            collected, how it is collected and how it is used. Except as
            described in the <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/dispute.html')">Dispute Policy</a>,
            information about domain name registrants other than their name and email address will
            be kept strictly confidential.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial" size="2">For full details, please view the full <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/privacy.dhtml')">Privacy
            Policy</a>.</font></p>
<h3><font face="Arial, Helvetica" color="#000080" size="2"><a name="TERMSOFUSE">Terms of Use</a></font></h3>
<p>The WebSite.ws <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/termsofuse.dhtml')">Terms of Use</a> covers all policies regarding the use of this site.  Please note that these <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/termsofuse.dhtml')">Terms of Use</a> are subject to change and that we may modify them from time to time without notice. We ask that you bookmark and periodically review this page to ensure continuing familiarity with the most current version of these <a href="javascript:OpenHelp('/glossary/termsofuse.dhtml')">Terms of Use</a>.  


</td>
